# Implementation Plan: BL-125 Final Mutation Audit

## Overview

Capstone validation that the immutable data model is fully enforced. No new production code --- only verification tests. Extends mutation guard tests to cover ALL entity types, verifies WriteContext() is only called from services, and confirms no form or ViewModel directly mutates entities.

## Tasks

- [ ] 1. Create comprehensive mutation audit test
  - [ ] 1.1 Create ComprehensiveMutationAuditTests class
    - Create OE2EmpireTracker.Tests/Services/ComprehensiveMutationAuditTests.cs
    - Test: AllEntityTypes_HaveMutationGuardCoverage --- verify every entity type has a mutation guard test file
    - Test: WriteContext_OnlyCalledFromServices --- grep for WriteContext() calls, assert only in service classes, PlayerContext, and test code
    - Test: NoFormDirectlyMutatesEntities --- grep Form*.cs files for entity property sets
    - Test: NoViewModelDirectlyMutatesEntities --- grep *ViewModel.cs files for entity property sets
    - Add Compile Include to test csproj
    - _Requirements: 1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 2.1, 2.2, 2.3, 3.1, 3.2, 4.1, 4.2, 4.3_

- [ ] 2. Verify all individual mutation guard tests exist
  - [ ] 2.1 Confirm mutation guard test files exist for all entity types
    - Blueprint, Colony, Survey, PlayerProfile, DeliveryRoute, PricingPlan, ShipTemplate, Ship, Station, BuildPlan, StockTarget, SupplyChain, Contacts, Asteroid
    - _Requirements: 1.1, 1.2_

- [ ] 3. Run full test suite and verify all pass
  - Build with zero errors and zero warnings
  - All tests pass including new comprehensive audit tests
  - node .kiro/tools/audit.js reports no new findings

## Notes

- No new production code --- test-only task
- This is the final validation step in the immutable data model migration
- If violations are found, they should be fixed in the relevant BL item, not in BL-125
- The comprehensive test complements (does not replace) individual mutation guard tests
